  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "77ecdaf0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Questions\n",
    "* Why more shots do not remove the readout error: The readout error is independent of the number of shots, and the recorded P(success) in this case should approach P = (1 - r)^2 = 0.97^2 = 0.9409 since two classical bits are read on Bob's side\n",
    "\n",
    "* Why we still need a preshared Bell pair + 1 qubit transmission: The Bell pair enables 4 possible orthogonal Bell states compared to a single qubit (which by the Holevo bound only can store 1 bit of information), and the 1 qubit transmission needs to happen because Bob's qubit is not directly affected by Alice's (i.e. his is still maximally mixed), meaning Bob will need both qubits (and the information encoded in their entanglement) to extract the information of the 2 classical bits."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b0699e75",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Part C: Deutsch–Jozsa"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "5b76fb7f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ORACLE_KINDS = [\"f=0\", \"f=1\", \"f=x0\", \"f=x1XORx0\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "def oracle_dj(oracle_kind):\n",
    "    o = QuantumCircuit(3, name=\"oracle\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # if f = 0, do nothing since y XOR 0 = y\n",
    "    if oracle_kind == \"f=0\":\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "\n",
    "    # if f = 1, always flip q2 since y XOR 1 = NOT y\n",
    "    elif oracle_kind == \"f=1\":\n",
    "        o.x(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # if f = x0, flip q2 if q0 = 1, else do nothing (equiv CNOT)\n",
    "    elif oracle_kind == \"f=x0\":\n",
    "        o.cx(0, 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # if f = x1 XOR x0, y XOR x1 XOR x0 is equivalent to x0 XOR (x1 XOR y)\n",
    "    # so y is flipped if x1 is 1, or x0 is 1\n",
    "    # y flipped twice if both are 1\n",
    "    elif oracle_kind == \"f=x1XORx0\":\n",
    "        o.cx(0, 2)\n",
    "        o.cx(1, 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return o\n",
    "\n",
    "def deutsch_jozsa(oracle_kind):\n",
    "    # q[0, 1] are input qubits, q2 is answer qubit\n",
    "    q = QuantumCircuit(3, 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # prepare 2nd qubit to ket(-)\n",
    "    q.x(2)\n",
    "    q.h(2)\n",
    "    q.barrier()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # place q0 and q1 in superposition\n",
    "    q.h([0, 1])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ask oracle\n",
    "    q.append(oracle_dj(oracle_kind), [0, 1, 2])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # measure q0 -> c0 and q1 -> c1\n",
    "    q.h([0, 1])\n",
    "    q.measure(0, 0)\n",
    "    q.measure(1, 1)\n",
    "    return q"
   ]
  },
