  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "066c9ed5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Questions\n",
    "* Role of phase kickback: Because q0 and q1 are in the ket(+) state (due to the H gates at the start), if the function is balanced, then the CNOT on q2 depends on if f=x0 or f=x1 XOR x0. This means that for either case, q0 (and q1 for the latter case) will \"pick up\" the negative phase from q2 since ket(-) is an eigenket of X and will flip the phase for the ket(1) in ket(+), transforming it to ket(-).\n",
    "\n",
    "* Role of the final H gates: Once the above kickback happens, the H gates will prepare q0 and q1 to be measured in the computational basis of Z. If the function is balanced, then at least one qubit in q0 or q1 will be ket(1), otherwise both will be ket(0).\n",
    "\n",
    "* Why is a noisy nonzero outcome no longer a conclusive test: If noise is introduced, then it is possible for readout or gate errors to perturbate the results such that a balanced function can appear to be constant and vice versa. One result is thus not sufficiently representative or conclusive of the nature of the unknown function and oracle"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f03c2991",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Part D: Grover Search"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "f7986d21",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def oracle():\n",
    "    # mark ket(10)\n",
    "    # so ket(10) -> X(1) -> ket(11) -> CZ(0, 1) -> -ket(11)\n",
    "    o = QuantumCircuit(2, name=\"oracle\")\n",
    "    o.x(1)\n",
    "    o.cz(0, 1)\n",
    "    o.x(1)\n",
    "    return o\n",
    "\n",
    "def diffuse():\n",
    "    d = QuantumCircuit(2, name=\"diffuse\")\n",
    "    d.h([0, 1])\n",
    "    d.x([0, 1])\n",
    "    d.cz(0, 1)\n",
    "    d.x([0, 1])\n",
    "    d.h([0, 1])\n",
    "    return d\n",
    "\n",
    "def grover_search(itera=1, redundant=0):\n",
    "    # assume ket(10) means q0 = ket(1), q1 = ket(0)\n",
    "    q = QuantumCircuit(2, 2)\n",
    "    q.h([0, 1])\n",
    "    q.barrier()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # add redundant CNOT pairs if need\n",
    "    for _ in range(redundant):\n",
    "        q.cx(0, 1)\n",
    "        q.cx(0, 1)\n",
    "    q.barrier()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # grover iters\n",
    "    for _ in range(itera):\n",
    "        o = oracle()\n",
    "        d = diffuse()\n",
    "        q.append(o, [0, 1])\n",
    "        q.append(d, [0, 1])\n",
    "        q.barrier()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # reverse the order due to the mapping\n",
    "    q.measure(0, 1)\n",
    "    q.measure(1, 0)\n",
    "    return q"
   ]
  },
